    declaration: type-alias-decl #156 10927:191:1-10988:192:1 name="@2::App" doc="The function that `serve` and `serve_tls` call for each request: the request with an empty `body`, the\n`RequestBody` that carries the body as it arrives, and the `Answer` out. A route that wants the body whole calls\n`read_all`; `app` makes an `App` from a `Handler`. A middleware is a function from an `App` to an `App`."
      target: type-ref #155 10938:191:12-10987:191:61 name="Fn"
        arg: type-ref #151 10941:191:15-10957:191:31 name="HttpWire.Request"
        arg: type-ref #152 10959:191:33-10970:191:44 name="@2::RequestBody"
        arg: type-ref #154 10972:191:46-10986:191:60 name="Result"
          arg: type-ref #153 10979:191:53-10985:191:59 name="@2::Answer"
    declaration: function-decl #194 12250:204:1-12664:217:1 name="@2::client" doc="Creates a client that keeps connections open and reuses them. `options` is optional and defaults to\n`HTTP.ClientOptions()`: 30 s timeouts, up to 4 connections, 1 MiB bodies, the system CA certificates and no proxy\n(set `tls: some(context)` to use a client context of `TLS.client_context` instead of the system certificates).\nEvery number in `options` must be positive, `max_connections` at most 65536 and `max_body_bytes` at most 64 MiB, or\nthe result is an error. With a `proxy` (`http://host:port`, an origin with no path) every `http://` request goes\nthrough that forward proxy in absolute form (`GET http://host/path HTTP/1.1`, `Host` still the target's), the\nconnections are pooled by the proxy. An `https://` request opens a `CONNECT host:port` tunnel through the proxy,\none per target, and speaks TLS inside it, verified against the target (a non-2xx answer to the `CONNECT` is an\nerror that names the proxy). A `proxy` that is not an `http://` origin is an error here. The user info of the\n`proxy` (`http://user:password@host:8080`, percent-decoded) is sent to the proxy as `Proxy-Authorization: Basic`,\nand a `407` from it is an error that names the proxy and not the credentials. Close the client with `close_client`."
      param: param #160 12261:204:12-12319:204:70 name="options"
        type: type-ref #158 12270:204:21-12292:204:43 name="HttpWire.ClientOptions"
        default: construct #159 12295:204:46-12319:204:70 type="HttpWire.ClientOptions"
      result: type-ref #162 12324:204:75-12347:204:98 name="Result"
        arg: type-ref #161 12331:204:82-12346:204:97 name="HttpWire.Client"
